New opt-in option `--modular-termination` (experimental, a first step that does not yet establish termination).  With it, `decreases {:global} E` declares a method's or function's global bound.  A call dispatched to a bodyless member of a trait whose implementations may lie in other modules is rejected unless the callee's global bound is below that of the member making the call.  This rejects only cycles whose dispatched calls are made directly by members with a bound.  A cycle through a helper method or function, or through a function value, is not detected, so a program can still prove `false` under the option.  With `--show-hints`, it reports every call that needs the rule.
